   "caption": {
    "en": "Why does Kolkata worship Kali on Diwali night? Kali Puja 2026 is on Sunday 8 November 🌑\n\nOn the new moon of Kartik, much of India worships Lakshmi. Bengal lights the lamps too, but we worship Kali, usually through the dark hours and often until dawn.\n\nIn the Devi Mahatmya she comes from Durga's brow to defeat Chanda and Munda. Dakshineswar draws huge crowds that night.\n\nThe full guide is on pujoparikramaguide.in.\n\nDoes your family do Kali Puja at home? Tell us in the comments 👇",
